  - m_Id: 610190500655104
    m_Localized: "The Spoliarium is Juan Luna\u2019s most enormous artwork in the
      Philippines. This monumental work of art won the gold medal during the 1884
      Madrid Exposition of Fine Arts."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 610308696141824
    m_Localized: "This painting is Hidalgo\u2019s interpretation of a violent and
      historical event involving Fernando Bustamante and the Spanish friars in Manila
      during the Spanish colonial period."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 610472546627584
    m_Localized: "Araw ng Kagitingan remembers The Fall of Bataan\u2014where over
      70,000 Filipino and American prisoners of war surrendered to the Japanese forces.
      Of this number, over 60,000 were Filipino soldiers. The surrender happened
      in Bataan, the last stand of the Filipino and American troops."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 610739056898048
    m_Localized: "Una Bulaque\xF1a, or The Woman from Bulacan, is one of Luna\u2019s
      paintings he did when he returned to the Philippines in 1894. Luna\u2019s expertise
      and excellence in the traditional style are manifested in this painting with
      her lifelike rendition of the details of the Bulaque\xF1a\u2019s pi\xF1a."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 610899212201984
    m_Localized: This series is composed of 14 oil paintings on canvas, considered
      to be the earliest known works of art to depict a historical event in the Philippines,
      the Basi Revolt of September 1807 in Ilocos.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
